      "computation_change_reason": "The conversion constant and resulting MGD flows are inputs to the critical dilution calculation; a different conversion factor or derived flow value would change dilution-based limit derivation."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/statement_of_basis.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 11, Section: fact_sheet",
      "exact_span": "The NMWQS for total residual chlorine (TRC) are 11 ug/l for chronic and 19 ug/l for acute conditions.",
      "affected_purpose": "A",
      "computation_change_reason": "These are the base water quality standards from which permit limits are derived; interpreting chronic versus acute applicability changes which numeric standard is selected."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/statement_of_basis.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 11, Section: fact_sheet",
      "exact_span": "The NNWQS for TRC are 4000 ug/L for domestic water supply, and primary/secondary human contact; 19 ug/L for aquatic & wildlife habitat-acute; and, 11 ug/L for aquatic & wildlife habitat-chronic and livestock watering.",
      "affected_purpose": "A",
      "computation_change_reason": "Multiple NNWQS values for different use classifications must be compared under the most-stringent-standard rule; interpretation of which use classifications apply to this discharge could change the selected limit."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/statement_of_basis.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 11, Section: fact_sheet",
      "exact_span": "Since acute conditions do not allow dilution; the limit must be met at end-of-pipe but chronic standards do allow dilution, the permit shall use the most stringent WQS for the permit limit.",
      "affected_purpose": "A",
      "computation_change_reason": "This rule governs whether dilution is permitted and which standard governs; different readings of acute versus chronic conditions or of the most-stringent-selection obligation would change the applicable enforceable limit."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/statement_of_basis.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 11, Section: fact_sheet",
      "exact_span": "Qe = facility effluent or design flow; 6.67 MGD",
      "affected_purpose": "A",
      "computation_change_reason": "Effluent flow is a direct input to the critical dilution formula; a different interpreted design or effluent flow would change the dilution factor and thus the derived limit."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/statement_of_basis.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 11, Section: fact_sheet",
      "exact_span": "Qa = 4Q3; 278.6 MGD",
      "affected_purpose": "A",
      "computation_change_reason": "Receiving-stream flow used as Qa in the critical dilution calculation; a different interpreted 4Q3 value would change the dilution factor and limit derivation."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/statement_of_basis.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 11, Section: fact_sheet",
      "exact_span": "F = fraction of stream allowed for mixing; 1.0",
      "affected_purpose": "A",
      "computation_change_reason": "The mixing-zone fraction is a multiplier in the critical dilution formula; interpreting whether 1.0 applies or a different fraction is authorized would change the computed limit."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/statement_of_basis.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 11, Section: fact_sheet",
      "exact_span": "The in-stream TRC concentration after allowing for dilution is; 11 ug/l ÷ 0.0234 = 470 ug/l. Since this value is greater than the 19 ug/l end-of-pipe acute standard, the 19 ug/l is more stringent and will be more protective.",
      "affected_purpose": "A",
      "computation_change_reason": "This passage records the comparison logic that selects the 19 ug/l limit over the dilution-adjusted chronic value; different interpretation of the comparison or arithmetic would change which numeric limit is deemed applicable."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/statement_of_basis.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 11, Section: fact_sheet",
      "exact_span": "The draft permit maintains the 19 ug/l end-of-pipe acute limit since it is more stringent and will be more protective than the 11 ug/l dilution based chronic limit.",
      "affected_purpose": "A",
      "computation_change_reason": "States the selected enforceable numeric limit for TRC; whether this 19 ug/l end-of-pipe limit is operative for compliance comparison directly determines Purpose A outcomes."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/statement_of_basis.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 11, Section: fact_sheet",
      "exact_span": "In addition to the 19 ug/l chemical specific limitation, the draft permit also maintains the narrative limit for total residual chlorine shall be “No Measurable.”",
      "affected_purpose": "A",
      "computation_change_reason": "A narrative no-measurable limit coexists with the 19 ug/l numeric limit; interpretation of whether both are independently enforceable, and how they interact, would change which limit applies to a given measurement."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/statement_of_basis.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 11, Section: fact_sheet",
      "exact_span": "TRC shall be limited as follows: “After dechlorination and prior to final disposal, the effluent shall contain NO MEASURABLE (TRC) at any time.",
      "affected_purpose": "A,C",
      "computation_change_reason": "The timing and process conditions ('after dechlorination and prior to final disposal') scope when the narrative limit applies; different interpretation of these conditions changes both the applicable limit (A) and how missing or conditional no-result periods are classified (C)."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/statement_of_basis.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 11, Section: fact_sheet",
      "exact_span": "NO MEASURABLE will be defined as no detectable concentration of TRC as determined by any approved method established in 40 CFR Part 136.",
      "affected_purpose": "A,C",
      "computation_change_reason": "The detection-limit-based definition determines what constitutes compliance or exceedance for the narrative limit and how non-detect or method-limited results should be interpreted when no ordinary numeric value is reported."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/statement_of_basis.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 11, Section: fact_sheet",
      "exact_span": "The effluent limitation for TRC is the instantaneous maximum and cannot be averaged for reporting purposes.",
      "affected_purpose": "A",
      "computation_change_reason": "The limitation type (instantaneous maximum, no averaging) governs how reported measurements must be compared to the limit; a different reading of averaging or reporting rules would change exceedance determinations."
    },
    {
      "source": "farmington/statement_of_basis.pdf",
      "locator": "Page 11, Section: fact_sheet",
      "exact_span": "The maximum dechlorinated TRC shall be monitored daily by grab sample.",
